Subject: [PATCH] viogpu3d: map GDI shadow and staging surfaces cached

The destination of every Blt present (a windowed D3D9 Present, a DirectDraw
Blt to the primary, a blt-model DXGI Present) is a shadow or staging
surface that dxgkrnl creates through GetStandardAllocationDriverData. These
live in guest RAM in segment 1, which is declared cache coherent, but the
allocation never set Flags.Cached, so VidMm mapped them write-combined. The
KMD's Venus Blt present writes them with the CPU, converting pixel by pixel
when the formats differ, and on hosts with an AMD CPU, whose KVM keeps the
guest's memory type, that ran at about 100 MB/s in the presenting thread's
kernel time: 16 ms per 640x480 Present, 38 ms at 1280x720. D3D9 at
interval one fell to 25 to 31 fps on helios.

Only these surfaces change (VIRGL_RESOURCE_FLAG_MAP_COHERENT, which the KMD
sets for exactly these two standard types). Marking every guest-RAM
allocation cached broke Venus device creation and is not done.

Evidence: docs/present.md, docs/evidence/present/.
Origin: vmlab-win3d present worker.
---
diff --git a/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_allocation.cpp b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_allocation.cpp
index d330c4e..6bbfb49 100644
--- a/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_allocation.cpp
+++ b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_allocation.cpp
@@ -870,6 +870,17 @@ NTSTATUS VioGpuAllocation::DxgkCreateAllocation(VioGpuAdapter *adapter, DXGKARG_
     allocationInfo->PreferredSegment.Direction0 = 0;
 
     allocationInfo->Flags.CpuVisible = TRUE;
+    /* Shadow and staging surfaces are the guest-RAM surfaces dxgkrnl
+     * creates for GDI and DWM, among them the destination of every Blt
+     * present, which DWM then reads with the CPU to compose the window. They
+     * live in segment 1, which is cache coherent: the host reaches guest RAM
+     * with the CPU. Without Cached, VidMm maps them write-combined, and every
+     * CPU read of them is uncached on hosts whose KVM honours the guest's
+     * memory type (AMD CPUs). */
+    if (!is_blob && allocation->IsCoherent())
+    {
+        allocationInfo->Flags.Cached = TRUE;
+    }
 #if VIOGPU_WDDM2
     /* Render and BLT Present still use physical allocation lists. WDDM 2
      * allocations referenced through those lists must explicitly permit
